# Settings page "Priority"
settings-priority = Priority
prio-title = Weights of the priority
prio-subtitle = The priority (0–100) orders the inbox: CVSS × weight plus EPSS percentile × weight, at most 100. A vulnerability in CISA KEV stays at least at the KEV floor. A match loses points when its assignment is uncertain or Debian or Ubuntu rate the vulnerability as minor.
prio-cvss = CVSS weight
prio-cvss-hint = 0 to 10 per CVSS point, default { $default }.
prio-epss = EPSS weight
prio-epss-hint = 0 to 100 for a percentile of 100 %, default { $default }.
prio-kev = KEV floor
prio-kev-hint = 0 to 100, default { $default }. Applies to matches of high or medium confidence.
prio-penalties = Deduction by confidence of the match
prio-medium = Medium
prio-low = Low
prio-penalties-hint = Points a match loses, default { $medium } and { $low }; high confidence loses nothing.
prio-recompute-hint = After saving, all priorities are recomputed in the background (about half a minute for all CVEs). Until then the instant mail waits; what the new weights lift above the thresholds counts as known and is not mailed afterwards.
prio-pending = The priorities are being recomputed. Lists and numbers may show old values until then.
prio-reset = Reset to defaults
prio-saved = Weights of the priority saved.
prio-examples = Examples with the current weights
prio-example-epss = EPSS percentile
prio-example-prio = Priority
prio-bands = Bands
prio-bands-hint = The bands of the priority are fixed.
prio-error-cvss = The CVSS weight must be a number between 0 and 10.
prio-error-epss = The EPSS weight must be a number between 0 and 100.
prio-error-kev = The KEV floor must be a whole number from 0 to 100.
prio-error-penalty = The deductions must be whole numbers from 0 to 100.
prio-error-order = Low confidence must not deduct less than medium.
prio-ratings = Deduction by the distribution's rating
prio-unimportant = Unimportant
prio-minor = Minor
prio-ratings-hint = Points a match of a package loses, default { $unimportant } and { $minor }. “Unimportant”: Debian “unimportant”, Ubuntu “negligible”. “Minor”: Debian “low” or no security update planned (no-dsa, postponed, ignored), Ubuntu “low”. KEV vulnerabilities stay at the KEV floor.
prio-error-rating-order = “Unimportant” must not deduct less than “Minor”.
